# Build & commit workflow

## Gulp tasks

| Task | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `setup-hooks` | Copy `pre-commit` / `post-commit` into `.git/hooks/` (executable) |
| `rename-js` | Always rename `scripts-*.js` and update HTML script refs |
| `rename-js-if-changed` | Rename + update HTML only if `assets/js/scripts-*.js` changed |
| `rename-css` | Always rename `main*.css` and update HTML stylesheet refs |
| `rename-css-if-changed` | Rename + update HTML only if `assets/css/main*.css` changed |
| `precommit` | Used by git hook: rename changed JS/CSS + version bump |
| `serve` (default) | BrowserSync on `./`, watches HTML/CSS/JS |
| `update-html` | Sync HTML script/stylesheet refs to current filenames (no rename) |

## Commit hooks

`pre-commit` → runs `yarn precommit` (`gulp precommit`):
1. If neither `assets/js/scripts-*.js` nor `assets/css/main*.css` has git changes → skip
2. Otherwise run `rename-js` and/or `rename-css` (timestamp rename + update all HTML refs)
3. `yarn version patch -i` (once, if either asset changed)
4. Stages generated changes

`post-commit` → stages any remaining changes and amends the commit (`git commit --amend --no-edit`).

## Yarn scripts

| Script | Command |
|--------|---------|
| `start` | `npx gulp` (BrowserSync on port 3000) |
| `setup-hooks` | Install git hooks from repo root |
| `ci` | `yarn install --immutable` (then `postci` runs `yarn start`) |
| `verify` | `yarn install --immutable --check-cache` |
| `precommit` | `gulp precommit` |
| `build:error-pages` | `node scripts/build-error-pages.js` — rebuild `404.html`, `403.html`, `500.html` from `contact.html` chrome |
| `test:e2e` | `playwright test` (local: requires `yarn start` on port 3000) |
| `test:e2e:headed` | Headed Edge run |
| `test:e2e:ui` | Playwright UI mode |
| `pretest:e2e` | Fails fast if nothing is listening on http://127.0.0.1:3000 |

**Package manager:** Yarn 4.17 (`packageManager` field). npm blocked via `engine-strict`.

## Playwright

- Config: `playwright.config.js` — Edge channel, `testDir: ./tests`
- CI: starts BrowserSync on port 3000 via `webServer`
- Local: run `yarn start` first, then `yarn test:e2e`
- Current tests: `tests/projects.spec.js` (New Masjid campaign page)

## Rules for agents

- **Never** manually edit `package.json` version
- **Never** manually change `scripts-{timestamp}.js` filename or HTML script `src`
- **Never** manually change `main-{timestamp}.css` filename or HTML stylesheet `href`
- After JS/CSS changes, verify with `yarn start` before committing
- Use `yarn ci` (`yarn install --immutable`) in CI; `yarn verify` checks install integrity

## Adding dependencies

Dev-only tooling belongs in `devDependencies`. Pin exact versions (`save-exact=true` in `.npmrc`).
